--- body ---
## Context
Every Claude Code session gets a scratch directory,
`/tmp/claude-<uid>/<cwd-key>/<session-id>/{scratchpad,tasks}`, and one
more per distinct cwd the session visits (an `EnterWorktree` mid-session
adds a second key). Verified on 2026-09-06 against the installed CLI
(2.1.263): the code only ever `mkdir`s that directory. There is no
delete-on-exit, no startup or periodic sweep, and no settings key. The
only relocation knob is the `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR` environment variable,
which takes precedence over `TMPDIR`. On doudou, an hour after a reboot,
13 session directories existed and 3 of their sessions were alive.

On doudou `/tmp` is a 12 GB tmpfs in RAM, mounted `usrquota`, and systemd
259 caps each user at 80 % of it at login. When agents point an arena or a
smoke run at their scratchpad (`smoke1130`, `matrix-hosted`, 1.9 GB on
2026-09-06), those directories outlive the session and count against every
later session of the same user. The 2026-09-06 fill (search-works-for-zotero
ticket 0714 names the main filler, an upstream test-suite leak) killed the
Bash tool in three sessions at once with EDQUOT and ended in a reboot. The
harness cannot fix third-party leaks; it can stop adding its own, and it
can see the fill coming.

## Relevant files
- `settings.json` — hook wiring; `SessionStart` runs `scripts/on-start.sh`, no `SessionEnd` entry exists
- `scripts/on-start.sh` — the pattern a `scripts/on-end.sh` would follow (declarative output, never non-zero)
- `skills/healthcheck/SKILL.md` — the numbered check list; a host-level temp check would be item 12
- `scripts/project-state.py` — the probe healthcheck reads; the new data (temp usage, orphan session dirs) belongs there so the skill stays a reader
- `skills/molt/SKILL.md` — the fix-now step; the orphan sweep is a repair, not a report
- `scripts/worktree-gc.sh` — existing liveness test for lock pids, the same test the sweep needs

## Actions
1. `SessionEnd` hook: a script that removes this session's own scratch
   directories (every `<cwd-key>/<session-id>` that matches the session id
   in the hook's JSON), never anything else. Ownership is clean by
   construction: no liveness test, no cross-session deletion. It covers
   every normal exit.
2. Healthcheck item 12, read from the probe: temp-root usage against the
   per-user cap where one applies, and the list of session directories
   whose session has no live process. `warn` when usage crosses a
   threshold or orphans exist; report-only.
3. Molt fix-now: delete the orphans the probe listed, gated on the same
   liveness test, one bullet per directory. Lair inherits both through
   the /molt it already calls (whose step 2 calls /healthcheck); roar
   does not, its own text disclaiming that scope. Add nothing to either
   skill.
4. Do not relocate the temp root from the harness. `CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR`
   is an operator decision (it also needs to stay short for sandbox
   socket paths), so document it in the healthcheck warning text rather
   than set it.

## Test
- Hook: spawn it via a real subprocess with a crafted `/tmp` fixture and a
  fake session id in the JSON; assert only that session's directories go,
  and a sibling session's survive. Red first: run against the tree before
  the hook exists and show the directory remains.
- Probe: a fixture temp root with one directory owned by a live pid and one
  by a dead pid; assert the probe lists exactly the dead one.

## Verification
- [x] Positive control: the hook test fails on the unfixed tree — measured
  2026-09-07 twice: against the tree with no `scripts/on-end.sh`, and against a
  no-op stub hook that exits 0 (the sharper control), where exactly the three
  behaviour-bearing assertions go red with the fixture directory still on disk
- [ ] After a normal session exit on doudou, the temp root no longer lists that
  session — NOT established in this run: the hook is wired in the tracked
  `settings.shared.json`, and the live per-machine `settings.json` is the
  operator's file (`check-settings-drift.sh` will report the drift). No session
  has exited under the new wiring yet
- [x] Healthcheck reports the temp line — probe run against the real root on
  doudou 2026-09-07: 25 session dirs, 5 live, 20 orphan, usage against the
  inferred per-user cap
- [ ] Molt removes a planted orphan and nothing else — established only on a
  hermetic fixture root (`test_sweep_removes_the_orphan_and_prunes_its_cwd_key`
  plus the live-vs-dead-pid test against the real `/proc`). No sweep was run
  against the live temp root: three sessions were working on this host and
  their scratch directories were in use
- [x] `tests/` pass; the SessionEnd script never exits non-zero (asserted on
  empty stdin, garbage, a blank id, a traversal id, and a missing temp root)

## Invariants
- No script ever deletes a directory whose session has a live process
- Hook output stays declarative; a hook failure prints nothing on every prompt
- Guard budget: this adds one hook and one probe field; retire nothing, since neither is a guard

## Exit criteria
- [x] `SessionEnd` hook wired and tested
- [x] Healthcheck item 12 and its probe field in place
- [x] Molt fix-now sweep in place, gated on liveness
- [x] `make check` passes
